I come home from my shift at the café.
The weather is beautiful and warm.
Sabine's small dog Bruno is waiting for me in the flat.
He is very happy.
I decide that we are going for a long walk.
I want to take him to the park.
I go to Sabine's bag and fetch the lead.
"Come here, Bruno!" I call.
He runs to me immediately.
I look at him and smile.
He jumps a little, but I stay calm.
"Sit!" I say strictly.
He sits down nicely.
He is not allowed to just run onto the street.
I attach the lead to his collar.
"Come, let's go!" I say happily.
We leave the flat together.
